        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "An investigation into the induction and action of the <i>lac</i> operon was carried out using the bacterium, <i>Escherichia</i> <i>coli</i>, grown in a growth medium containing glucose.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When the bacteria had used all the glucose, an excess of lactose was added to the growth medium. The activity of β-galactosidase was measured from this time (0 min), as shown in Fig. 3.1.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig3.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 3.1",
            "src": "figures/q3_fig3_1.png",
            "alt": "Beta-galactosidase activity",
            "source": {
              "qp": 6
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "With reference to the <i>lac</i> operon, explain the shape of the curve in Fig. 3.1.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 7,
        "topics": [
